## M20 commit message
KS-991: skip a local develop that origin/develop provably supersedes (#903)

* KS-991: skip a LOCAL develop that origin/develop provably supersedes

Three pushes in one session ran the full 13-leg Blockchain/Dev preflight on
branches touching no Blockchain/Dev file, because the local `develop` ref was
behind `origin/develop` and the hook's base loop consults it first:

    ff5218867 vs 400517aaf    (systemTest-only branch)
    400517aaf vs 4f337be83    (CLAUDE.md-only branch)
    4f337be83 vs 512480ef1    (one new file)

Every gap was opened by a merge the same seat had just performed, so the trigger
is "you did the right thing". One of those runs then failed leg 1 with
DEPS MISSING — an environment condition presented as a gate result and, without
reading 13 legs of output, indistinguishable from a real red. That is the shape
that gets answered with --no-verify.

NOT A REORDER, and that distinction is the whole justification. KS-882's author
considered putting origin/develop first and rejected it, because whichever ref is
consulted FIRST can contain HEAD. This skips a ref only when ANOTHER resolvable
ref provably supersedes it — local `develop` when it is a strict ancestor of
origin/develop. The two failure directions are opposites:

    KS-882  a ref CONTAINING the tip  -> empty diff    -> HIDES a change
    KS-991  a ref BEHIND the remote   -> inflated diff -> INVENTS a change

A stale base sits at or behind the better base, so its diff is a SUPERSET: it can
report files that are on the trunk but not in this branch, and it cannot conceal
anything. Skipping it costs no safety.
